{
  "dom_id": "step-q38861",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})=-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2},\\,$ $T({b}_{2})={c}_{1}-4{c}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{3})=5{c}_{1}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we write the images of vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})={c}_{1}-4{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{3})=5{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2})$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
      "key": "selection",
      "type": "radio",
      "choices": [
        {
          "option": "a",
          "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-38861-a",
